":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:38:55Z","updated_at":"2026-09-24T17:29:06Z","closed_at":"2026-09-24T17:29:05Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.7.2 and 4.8dev6\n\n### System information\n\nGoogle Pixel 9 Pro\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm using the official Perfetto templates for 4.7.2 and built them myself for 4.8dev6.\nThe game loads into the main menu without an issue. However, once I switch to a scene that contains nodes with `Sub Thread` processing mode, the game crashes. I can fix it by switching these nodes to `Main Thread` at which point the game runs as expected.\nEven further, if I remote deploy to the phone with `Main Thread` processing, I can load the crashing scene. But as soon as I switch the processing mode to `Sub Thread` in the editor, the remote deployed game crashes.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI could narrow it down to having at least two nodes with `Sub Threaded` set and accessing any of the `Engine` methods in its `_process` method. Something like this:\n```\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tEngine.get_frames_per_second()\n```\nI can reproduce it as well with `Time` so seems to be a general issue with engine provided singletons.\n\nFor the MRP it's enough to use the official Perfetto template and then do a remote deploy. It instantly crashes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[perfetto-crash.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32288023/perfetto-crash.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.